fm1-midi-bridge: licensing

This tree mixes code under four licences and builds against binary-only libraries.
Each source file carries an SPDX-License-Identifier line that is the authority
for that file; this file is the map. The full licence texts are in LICENSES/;
THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md lists what a release's binaries carry; tools/release.sh
puts both next to the packages of every release.

1. MIT (our code)

   Everything written for this project: app/midi/, app/bridge.c, app/ui/ (except
   the two font headers, below), app/input/, app/settings.c, app/update/,
   app/fm1_log.c, app/health.c, app/util/, app/bt_ble/ble_port.c, adv_parse.c,
   ble_host.h, app/usb/usb_port.c, app/minimal.c, tests/, tools/ (except
   tools/fm1pkg_make.py, and see tools/fm1_install_paced.py and tools/trs_tester/
   below), web/editor.html and docs/.

   Copyright (c) 2026 ForrestPanda

   Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy
   of this software and associated documentation files (the "Software"), to deal
   in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights
   to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell
   copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is
   furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:

   The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in
   all copies or substantial portions of the Software.

   THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR
   IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,
   FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE
   AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER
   LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,
   OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN
   THE SOFTWARE.

   tools/fm1_install_paced.py is MIT on its own but imports and subclasses
   Felucca's fm1_install.py (GPL-3.0-only, not in this tree): the program that
   runs is a combination under the GPL-3.0-only.

   tools/trs_tester/usb_descriptors.c is adapted from TinyUSB's midi_test example,
   Copyright (c) 2019 Ha Thach (tinyusb.org), MIT: its notice is kept in the file
   and in LICENSES/MIT-TinyUSB.txt. The tester also links TinyUSB (MIT).

2. Apache License 2.0 (code derived from the JieLi AC79 AIoT SDK)

   app/app_main.c, app/Makefile, app/board/, app/include/, app/bt_ble/ble.c,
   ble_midi.c, ble_midi.h and ble_host.c (derived from the SDK's demo_ble,
   le_trans_data.c and le_net_central.c; the last two carry JieLi's own notice,
   kept at the top of our files), and app/usb/ except usb_port.c (the USB-MIDI
   device class, written after the SDK's cdc.c and hid.c, and the composite-device
   and descriptor files with a MIDI branch) are derived from the SDK's sources
   (https://gitee.com/Jieli-Tech/fw-AC79_AIoT_SDK, tag AC79NN_SDK_V1.2.1_2023-12-13),
   which JieLi publishes under the Apache License, Version 2.0. The licence text
   is LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt (also at http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0).
   Changes are noted at the top of each file.

3. GNU GPL version 3 (a build tool, not linked into the firmware)

   tools/fm1pkg_make.py is our fork of Felucca's packager, Copyright (C) 2026
   Leo Kuroshita (@kurogedelic), Hügelton Instruments, GPL-3.0-only
   (https://github.com/hugelton/Felucca), modified 2026-10-11 as its header says.
   It runs on the host at packaging time only. The licence text is
   LICENSES/GPL-3.0-only.txt.

   The .fwsc package it produces also contains Felucca's update loader (ota.bin,
   GPL-3.0-only), unmodified, built from firmware/loader/ of Felucca tag v1.6
   (commit 1727537624390cc3f9c7dff2456b43b3a8edb005): a separate program the
   FM-1's SPL runs during an install, never linked with the bridge. Its complete
   corresponding source, the whole Felucca tree at that tag, is attached to every
   release as felucca-v1.6-source.tar.gz next to the packages, and is at
   https://github.com/hugelton/Felucca/tree/v1.6. Nothing under the GPL is
   compiled or linked into the bridge firmware.

4. Bitstream Vera Fonts licence (the panel fonts)

   app/ui/font.h and app/ui/font_big.h are bitmaps of DejaVu Sans Mono glyphs
   rendered by tools/mkfont.py: a modified copy of the Bitstream Vera font
   software, Copyright (c) 2003 by Bitstream, Inc. All Rights Reserved.
   Bitstream Vera is a trademark of Bitstream, Inc. DejaVu changes are in the
   public domain. The notice is in each header and in LICENSES/Bitstream-Vera.txt.

5. Binary-only libraries (not in this tree, not ours to license)

   The firmware links JieLi's Bluetooth, USB and kernel libraries, shipped
   without source as binary .a files in the AC79 SDK. JieLi publishes that SDK
   repository, the libraries included, as an open-source project under the
   Apache License 2.0 (the LICENSE at the top of
   https://gitee.com/Jieli-Tech/fw-AC79_AIoT_SDK, tag
   AC79NN_SDK_V1.2.1_2023-12-13). They are not included here; a build needs
   the SDK checkout. A binary package of this firmware carries their code, and
   is redistributed under those terms. The third-party code known to be inside
   them (micro-ecc, BSD 2-Clause; newlib; FreeRTOS; LLVM compiler-rt) and the
   SDK's three boot files in every package are listed, with their notices, in
   THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md.

The FM-1 hardware, its stock firmware and the names M-VAVE and FM-1 belong to
their owners. This project is not affiliated with M-VAVE.
